WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.569
-As we've seen repeatedly
over the last few months,

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:06.106
when the Trump administration
is confronted with facts

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.440
that don't support their agenda,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.509
they try to discredit
the sources of those facts,

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.977
and right now,
they're using that same strategy

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.178
on healthcare.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.347
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:18.017
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:20.820
Of course, since basically
the beginning of his campaign,

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.822
Trump has tried to undermine
the press

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.290
as the source of information.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.260
In fact, even when he's making
small talk with world leaders,

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.096
he can't help but make sarcastic
comments about the media.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.565
On Tuesday, he held a photo op
in the Oval Office

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.566
with the crown prince
of Saudi Arabia,

00:00:34.566 --> 00:00:36.136
and it was super awkward.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.370
[ Camera shutters clicking ]

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.573
-They're very nice people.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.742
-We hope so.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:44.276 --> 00:00:46.379
[ Audience laughs ]

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.718
-Are you guys
in the White House,

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.285
or on a terrible first date?

00:00:53.285 --> 00:00:54.721
[ Audience laughs ]

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.189
-[ As Trump ] Do you always
wear that thing on your head?

00:00:57.189 --> 00:00:59.158
-[ As bin Salman ] I do.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:01.093
Do you always wear that thing
on<i> your</i> head?"

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:02.895
[ Audience laughs ]

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:06.332
[ Normal voice ] Of course...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.167
Of course,
Trump dislikes the media

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.069
because they often report
basic facts

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.472
that challenge his world view
for the same reason

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.507
his administration now dislikes
the Congressional Budget Office,

00:01:15.507 --> 00:01:17.010
which released a damning report

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.145
on the Republican
healthcare plan on Monday

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.980
that projected the bill
would cause

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.083
a stunning 24 million Americans
to lose coverage.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.152
Now, that might seem like
a disaster,

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.387
but House Speaker Paul Ryan
actually tried to spin it

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:30.623
as a positive,
prompting skepticism

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.692
even from straight-laced
Fox News anchor Bret Baier.

00:01:33.692 --> 00:01:35.929
-If you read this entire report,
I'm pretty encouraged by it.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.697
I'm excited about this analysis.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.598
And I'm really, actually,
frankly encouraged.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:42.902
-Mr. Speaker, if you're
<i> encouraged</i> by this CBO report,

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.571
what's a CBO report
you're<i> discouraged</i> by?

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:46.872
[ Audience laughs ]

00:01:46.872 --> 00:01:48.974
That's the closest Bret Baier
has ever come to saying,

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:50.242
"Bye, Felicia."

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:51.578
[ Audience laughs ]

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.313
Also, Paul Ryan,

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.848
you're encouraged
that 24 million people

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.350
will be thrown off
their insurance?

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.252
Is that really the word
you want to use,

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.888
or are you thinking
of a different E-word?

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.189
-Excellent.
-There it is.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.523
[ Audience laughs ]

00:02:04.523 --> 00:02:07.293
So how can Paul Ryan say
he's encouraged by this report?

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.429
Well, he makes several
misleading claims.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.630
For example, Ryan says
the report confirms

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.465
that the bill
will lower premiums,

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:16.502
which is technically true, but
only for young, healthy people.

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.938
Older people would see
their premiums skyrocket.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:22.441
In fact, the CBO report finds
that the average 64-year-old

00:02:22.441 --> 00:02:26.779 line:0%
earning $26,500 would see
their premiums go up from $1,700

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.615 line:0%
to $14,600 a year.

00:02:29.615 --> 00:02:31.751
So get ready to start
running into your grandpa

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.485
working at Subway.

00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:35.254
-[ As old man ]
When I was a kid,

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.857
12-inch Italians weren't even
allowed in the country!

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:39.692
[ Audience laughs ]

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.994
[ Normal voice ] So, Paul Ryan
has chosen the strategy

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:44.063
of trying to make the CBO report
sound positive,

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.831
and what about Trump
and his surrogates?

00:02:45.831 --> 00:02:48.668
They're just saying we shouldn't
believe the CBO at all --

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.304
Like CNN commentator and Trump
supporter Jeffrey Lord,

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:53.238
who tried to discredit
the CBO report

00:02:53.238 --> 00:02:55.608
by making an analogy
that didn't quite hold up.

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.376
-We don't know what
the weather's gonna be.

00:02:57.376 --> 00:02:59.512
It's gonna snow, but how much?
I mean, we don't know.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.046
We don't trust weathermen,
you know,

00:03:01.046 --> 00:03:02.281
so why should we trust the CBO?

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:03.482
All right, first of all,

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:04.950
the reason we don't trust
weathermen is because

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.686
they have names like
Dallas Rains or Storm Tornado.

00:03:07.686 --> 00:03:08.654
[ Audience laughs ]

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.323
And second of all,
in this analogy,

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.590
if the CBO is the weatherman,

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:13.626
then that makes Donald Trump
this kid.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.095
-Dewpoints in the 20s
and near 30 degrees

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.230
across central Mississippi.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.564
Well, hey there.

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:21.333
-I don't know what's going on,
but Zayn doesn't know.

00:03:21.333 --> 00:03:25.104
Are you sure?
Are you crazy sure?!

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:28.307
-[ Chuckles nervously ] Well...
-Ca-caw! Ca-caw!

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:30.810
-We've got a little bit
of interesting things

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.245
going on right now.
-Ffft! Pbht!

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.013
-Take a look at what's
going on right now.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.548
You want to point out
the weather right now?

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:38.551
-Yeah, there are farts
everywhere and toots!

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.886
I don't even know! It's crazy!

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:42.855
[ Audience laughs, applause ]

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:45.958
-You can laugh...

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:47.493
You can laugh, but Donald Trump

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.461
just made that kid
Secretary of Weather.

00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:50.996
[ Audience laughs ]

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:53.899
And then yesterday,
White House Spokesman/Hostage,

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:57.370
Sean Spicer, also tried
to discredit the CBO report.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.772
Spicer tried to claim
that the new GOP bill

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:02.775
was only the first part of
a three-part healthcare plan,

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.743
meaning the CBO's report
was inaccurate

00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:06.279
because it didn't
take into account

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:09.014
future legislation
that doesn't exist yet.

00:04:09.014 --> 00:04:11.550
And he kept using one word
in particular.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.786
-The comprehensive nature
of the three-pronged plan...

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.621
In prongs two and three...

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:17.290
Doing the first prong of this...

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.925
On the first prong alone...

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.659
Prong one of three prongs...

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:22.328
But the second prong of this...

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.963
So, prong two is actually
fairly easy to do.

00:04:24.963 --> 00:04:28.267
The third prong...
This piece of this prong only...

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:31.036
Without looking
at prong two and three...

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:34.940
-Wait, is "prong"
Sean Spicer's safe word,

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.143
and he forgot to tell everyone?
[ Audience laughs ]

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:40.112
Prong! You guys, prong!

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:42.681
I'm gonna go back to
the Oval Office, but prong!

00:04:42.681 --> 00:04:44.083
[ Audience laughs ]

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:46.785
Of course, as usual, Trump
is doing a complete 180 here,

00:04:46.785 --> 00:04:49.421
because he used to love
the Congressional Budget Office

00:04:49.421 --> 00:04:50.890
when it suited his needs,

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:54.761
tweeting about the CBO at least
13 times to criticize Obama.

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:57.362
The only constant in all of this
is that Trump likes something

00:04:57.362 --> 00:04:59.765
if it agrees with him
and he hates it if it doesn't.

00:04:59.765 --> 00:05:01.834
Take for example
the monthly jobs report.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:04.537
Trump famously used to call
the unemployment rate "phony,"

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:05.704
but now that he's president,

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:07.139
he's bragging about
the jobs numbers.

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:09.608
So how does the White House
explain the flip flop?

00:05:09.608 --> 00:05:11.543
Sean Spicer had this to say
last week.

00:05:11.543 --> 00:05:13.345
-I talked to the president
prior to this,

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:15.013
and he said to quote him
very clearly.

00:05:15.013 --> 00:05:17.517
They may have been phony in the
past, but it's very real now.

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:20.153
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:21.120
-Oh, my God.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.521
[ Audience laughs ]

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:24.089
We're so pronged.

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:26.926
[ Audience laughs ]

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:30.729
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:34.400
Even when Trump makes a claim
in his own words,

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.168
like when he accused
President Obama

00:05:36.168 --> 00:05:37.937
of wiretapping him,
we can't be sure

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.705
if we're supposed to actually
take him literally.

00:05:39.705 --> 00:05:41.574
Remember, Trump tweeted,
"Terrible!

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:44.510
Just found out that Obama had my
'wires tapped' in Trump Tower."

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.246
And "President Obama was tapping
my phones in October."

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:49.882
And, yet, when Spicer was asked
if Trump had any proof

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.517
that Trump was indeed
wiretapped,

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:52.785
Spicer responded with this.

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.319
-He doesn't really think
that President Obama

00:05:54.319 --> 00:05:56.355
went up and tapped his phone
personally.

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:58.424
The president
"used the word wiretapped"

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.459
in quotes to mean, broadly,

00:06:00.459 --> 00:06:02.294
surveillance
and other activities.

00:06:02.294 --> 00:06:05.330
-Because what is "wiretap"
if not a cool slang term

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.366
that means a bunch
of different things like,

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:09.134
"We should wiretap some molly"

00:06:09.134 --> 00:06:11.737
or "I want to wiretap dat ass."

00:06:11.737 --> 00:06:12.905
[ Audience laughs ]

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:15.441
Now, today, the Attorney General
Jeff Sessions,

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:18.410
who would know if there was
any evidence of wiretapping,

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:21.714
was asked if he had provided any
such evidence to the president,

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:23.249
and he seemed flustered.

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:33.960
-Um...

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.828
Look, um...

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:37.296
The answer is no.

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:39.097
Um, but, um...

00:06:39.097 --> 00:06:41.300
-[ As Sessions ] Well,
you better get that man

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.136
some sweet tea
and a porch to sit on,

00:06:43.136 --> 00:06:47.039
because he is sweating more
than a gator in a boot store!

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:48.975
[ Audience laughs ]

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:50.376
[ Normal voice ] So,
Trump's own attorney general

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:52.044
couldn't give us any evidence,

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:54.947
then there was the Republican
overseeing the investigation

00:06:54.947 --> 00:06:56.315
in the House, Devin Nunes,

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:58.951
who offered a similar argument
to Spicer,

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:01.720
claiming Obama didn't personally
go to Trump Tower

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:03.155
and put in a wiretap.

00:07:03.155 --> 00:07:05.424
-We don't have any evidence that
that took place.

00:07:05.424 --> 00:07:08.427
I don't think there was
an actual tap of Trump Tower.

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:10.596
President Obama
wouldn't physically go over

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.898
and wiretap Trump Tower,

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:15.334
so now you have to decide,
as I mentioned to you last week,

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:18.638
are you gonna take the tweets
literally, and if you are,

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:20.773
then clearly the President
was wrong.

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:25.077
-Stop telling us Obama didn't
physically go to Trump Tower!

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:27.079
Nobody thought that!

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:29.181
[ Audience laughing ]
[ As Obama ] Uh, hello!

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:32.785
I'm here...

00:07:32.785 --> 00:07:37.890
I'm, uh, here from
A.T. and, uh...T.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.224
[ Audience laughs ]

00:07:39.224 --> 00:07:42.694
[ Normal voice ]
So, sometimes Trump is pro-CBO,

00:07:42.694 --> 00:07:44.230
other times he's anti-CBO,

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:45.831
sometimes he says
the jobs numbers are phony,

00:07:45.831 --> 00:07:47.032
other times says they're real,

00:07:47.032 --> 00:07:48.567
sometimes he says things
in quotes,

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:50.135
other times
he really means them,

00:07:50.135 --> 00:07:51.804
but one thing we do know

00:07:51.804 --> 00:07:53.639
is we can't believe his promises
on healthcare,

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:55.341
like when he promised
during the campaign

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:57.376
that he wouldn't let people
suffer as president,

00:07:57.376 --> 00:08:00.980
using one favorite phrase
over and over again.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.381
-I said,
"Nobody's going to be dying

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.016
on the street if I'm president.

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.551
-Did you say you're a liberal
on healthcare?

00:08:05.551 --> 00:08:07.486
-I will not let people die on
the streets if I'm president.

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:09.955
People are not gonna
die in the middle of the street.

00:08:09.955 --> 00:08:12.124
People are not gonna
die on the sidewalk.

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:14.660
You're not gonna let people die

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.562
sitting in the middle
of a street.

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.798
-Why does he think people
are walking out

00:08:18.798 --> 00:08:21.600
to the middle of the street
to die?

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:24.503
Must...make it to street!

00:08:24.503 --> 00:08:26.138
[ Audience laughing ]

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:29.774
Sit down in middle of street!

00:08:29.774 --> 00:08:32.612
And die with dignity!

00:08:32.612 --> 00:08:34.980
So, Trump made huge promises
on healthcare

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.515
that he clearly had no intention
of keeping.

00:08:36.515 --> 00:08:40.019
His bill would cut Medicare
and kick millions off insurance.

00:08:40.019 --> 00:08:42.488
If it passes, we're all
gonna need a safe word.

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:43.922
-Prong. Prong. Prong. Prong.

00:08:43.922 --> 00:08:45.824
Prong. Prong. Prong.
Prong. Prong. Prong.

00:08:45.824 --> 00:08:47.727
-[ To the tune of "Thong Song" ]
♪ Prong, p-prong, prong, prong ♪

00:08:47.727 --> 00:08:49.762
[ Audience laughs ]
That's been "A Closer Look."

00:08:49.762 --> 00:08:52.231
[ Cheers and applause ]

